  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSurface high pressure continues to build into the area, with \nnights starting to get a little longer and some boundary layer \nmoisture in place, valley fog will could develop in the \novernight hours, lasting through sunrise, across the Twin Tiers \nof NY and PA. Daily high temperatures expected to be 80s Friday\nthrough Sunday, and in the upper 70s today.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nThe weather pattern will turn more active late in the weekend and \ninto early next week as a broad upper level trough digs into the \nNortheast US. There are some storm ingredients lining up during\nthe early week, with a few hundred J/kg of CAPE and over 25\nknots of bulk shear, and PWATs around 1-1.5 inches. Overall, it\nwill be a more active period in the early week, but ingredient\nvalues are lower than over the past few weeks. Temperatures will\nremain seasonable through next week.",
